WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:12.480
Hi, welcome back to our Wheel of Life
online retreat.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:22.440
We've reached our third session. By the way, I apologize the meditation in the second section went on too long.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.480
Let's try to set a timer this time.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.040
So, there's a tradition
when you teach the steps to the path

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:47.320
that you try to connect this whole retreat
to the last retreat you did

00:00:53.360 --> 00:01:04.240
So, for online session 3, we're going to review
where we left off in the last retreat.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:21.880
I think it was in Bali with many friends there.
So, we're studying the medium person's motivation.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:37.080
They want to get out of all troubled life.
They want to reach Nirvana.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.840
By the way, it doesn't mean they want to disappear;

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.960
just their life becomes perfect,
and they don't have a single problem in this life.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:02:01.720
That's like getting out of the jail, but there's a famous joke in the steps to the path--lam rim (LAM RIM).

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:10.960
If you don't know you're in the jail,
you don't want to get out of the jail.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.040
So, we have to talk about why we are in the jail,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:29.760
and we've reached the part in the lam rim
where we talk about dying,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:41.480
which is kind of like going from one cell
in the jail to the other cell in the jail.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:57.040
But, if you understand how each cell door works
then you can break out of the jail.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:08.400
So, we're going to talk about how do people
die and what happens when you die.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.160
And we've reached a very important part
of the death process,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:26.000
which is called sundep-pa (GSOS 'DEBS PA).
And, in these lam rim teachings

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:32.120
I'm going to sprinkle in some
Tibetan and Sanskrit words.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.280
Stanley will turn them into traditional Chinese words,

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:50.080
and I think it's going to make your experience deeper,
so please don't be afraid of the foreign words.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:59.280
Every word you learn will increase your knowledge

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:13.600
and that will increase your ability to break out of the jail. So, here's the Tibetan and I'll pronounce it.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:23.840
sundep yul ni, le kar nak mangpoy nang ne
(GSOS 'DEBS YUL NI, LAS DKAR NAG MANG PO'I NANG NAS)  So, when you're about to die

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.920
there's like a lottery that goes on in your mind

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:44.440
So, in your brain there are many, many, many seeds
that you collected during your lifetime.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:52.600
Some are good seeds, some are bad seeds,
and actually there are millions of those seeds.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:04.680
Now, just at the crucial moment of death,
of the rough state of mind in death--

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:18.200
your mind picks one of those karmas,
out of millions,

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:28.440
and when it picks it, it's kind of like
it turns on the timer for a bomb.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:42.800
So, you saw those hero movies,
like [chinese movie name],

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:49.360
or the famous American movies... like Iron Man

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:04.000
The bad guy sets a nuclear bomb. He turns on a timer.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:17.360
Maybe it's a 60-minute timer, and the good hero has
60 minutes to stop the bomb.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:29.000
So, that timer is actually a smaller bomb.
And when the time runs out,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.640
the smaller bomb goes off and it
triggers the bigger bomb.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:48.560
So, in Tibetan the word sundep-pa (GSOS 'DEBS PA) means to put on the timer,

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:58.400
and that will cause the bomb to explode.
And in this case, the bomb is your next life.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:05.920
So, just as you are dying,

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:18.480
they turn on the seeds in your mind ...
timer ... and then that seed will blow up.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:27.000
And it will push you into a next life.
Now, so it's very important to choose the right seed.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:43.720
And there is a  system about those seeds, and that was the last thing we studied in the lam rim in Bali,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.920
last December.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:59.680
We talked about who decides what seed is
going to be selected in the lottery.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:10.680
And in this lam rim book we had three decisions.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:23.280
First one:  le kang top che-wa
(LAS GANG STOBS CHE BA).

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.240
It means: who decides which seed will open first?

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:34.760
Then I'll ask you a question.
Well, which seed is more powerful?

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:42.640
A powerful bad seed would be like you killed somebody.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:50.040
Or a powerful good seed you save someone's life,
one time in your whole life.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:09:03.280
And I have saved a person's life. It's the greatest feeling in the world and you never forget it.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:10.520
So, first principle. What was the most powerful seed?
So, first principle. What was the most powerful seed?

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.040
Okay, second principle.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:21.200
de nyam na, kang kom-pa che-wa dang
(DE MNYAM NA, GANG GOMS PA CHE BA DANG)

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.320
If the power of the two seeds is equal,

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.560
which one will open first?

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:39.760
And I don't know, let's say you told a big lie in your life,

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:47.000
but you also criticized someone very badly in your life.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:57.320
And karmically, to tell a big lie
and to give a big criticism to somebody,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.280
those two karmas are almost equal.
So, which one will open first?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:17.760
They can't open at the same time; one has to open first. Then he says kom-pa che-wa (GOMS PA CHE BA),

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.480
it means: which one are you more used to doing?

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:31.920
Are you a person who who likes to
lie all the time to people,

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:39.040
or are you an angry person who criticizes other people?

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:47.120
Then, if the time comes for those two
seeds to open--lying and criticizing--

00:10:51.240 --> 00:11:05.080
then which one you did more often as a habit in your life, that seed will be selected at the moment of death.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:13.640
Okay, and then the text says: de nyam na,

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.800
kang ngun la che-pa
(DE MNYAM NA, GANG SNGON LA BYAS PA).

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.160
Good, his Tibetan is getting quite good.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:30.960
So, suppose the habit is equal.
And suppose the power of that karma's equal.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:36.560
Well, then which one did you do first?

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:44.480
Which one came before the other?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:51.200
de nyi la sundep so (DE NYID LA GSOS 'DEBS SO).
That one will be selected.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:59.920
Now, there's a very, very, very, very, very, very famous book about emptiness,

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:06.400
which is called Gomba Rabsel (DGONGS PA RAB GSAL),

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:19.360
which means "I will illuminate for you
what Chandrakirti and Nagarjuna
really meant about emptiness."

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:39.240
And that book is by Je Tsongkapa,
and I think it's maybe the greatest book he ever wrote.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.160
And he asked the same question:

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:53.120
which karma will be selected, which timer will be set?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.840
And he gives a little bit more detailed explanation.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:09.600
And that comes from an Abhidharma text.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:19.120
Abhidharma is some of the most ancient
teachings of Buddhism in this world...

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.000
very difficult.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:34.920
Stanley is actually translating the most famous book;
he's scheduled to finish in 2046.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:44.040
And in that book, there's a poem

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:49.680
and it's supposed to be by the Buddha.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:56.680
And I wanted to give that to you.
I will do that during these lam rim teachings.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:11.720
If I think some idea's very important;
like "which seeds can I open first when I die?"

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:16.200
To me, that's a very
important question.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:24.400
So, sometimes I will go deeper
on a question from another book,

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:31.200
and that's why these retreats take so long.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:36.520
It's to help you in your life.

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:43.120
So, I'd like to take this poem from
Vasabandhu and from Buddha.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:53.880
le kyi korwar chi kang dang,
nye-wa kang dang kom-pa kang,
ngun che kang yin de dak le,
nga ma nga ma rnam min gyur,

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:54.280
(,LAS KYIS 'KHOR BAR LCI GANG DANG,
,NYE BA GANG DANG GOMS PA GANG,
,SNGON BYAS GANG YIN DE DAG LAS,
,SNGA MA SNGA MA RNAMS SMIN 'GYUR,)

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.800
is the poem.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.040
le kyi korwar chi kang dang...

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:09.560
le kyi korwar chi kang dang means:
when the karma makes you spin in the wheel,

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:22.520
there's a certain priority system.
Some seeds have to open before other seeds.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:30.320
And that depends on certain factors.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:35.320
chi kang (LCI GANG) means:
which karma is more serious?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:43.160
Killing someone is more serious than lying to someone.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:53.080
Then it says nye-wa kang (NYE BA GANG).
Which one is closer?

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:58.760
And this is a very, very important idea,

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:05.560
which we'll talk more about in future
segments of this lam rim.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:20.760
But "closer" means, "closer to the moment of death."
So, certain kinds of karma,

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:28.080
even though maybe they are not as
serious as other karmas,

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:38.160
but if you do them closer to the moment
of your death and passing on,

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:53.200
then they will take priority. Like, if you have a great desire on the last day of your life

00:16:54.280 --> 00:17:03.920
it can change which karmic timer is put on,
and we'll talk about it.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:10.360
Then it says kom-pa kang (GOMS PA GANG),
which one did you do more frequently?

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:21.000
Which one did you get used to
because you used to do it a lot?

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:28.480
And, one thing I don't like about these online classes ...

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:38.520
I like to quiz my students and offer reward money,

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:58.040
so I don't get to do it in the online class.
So, this class is going to be cheaper for me,
but it's fun for me to do that kind of gambling.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:06.000
Maybe, I'll ask Stanley.
So, here it says kom-pa (GOMS PA),

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:16.000
and it's pronounced kom-pa, kom-pa. Yeah, and
it means "you got used to something,"

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:19.880
"you got a habit."

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:28.680
Then there's another Tibetan word for $100 ...
so all of you are not going to get money,

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:33.800
only Stanley and Allison will get money
during this lam rim.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:39.640
I think if they don't get it correct,
they should give me the money.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:47.840
Okay, so if you change the pronunciation...
kom-pa means "to get used to something."

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.640
For $100, Stanley,

00:18:54.680 --> 00:19:03.120
maybe we could have him represent someone in the audience ... what's the verb gom-pa (SGOMS PA) mean?

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.360
Sounds almost the same.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:19.000
Yeah, "meditation.  "Hundred dollars!  So, I'll give you a hundred dollars.  Stop answering all of them.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:27.040
Okay, so it's very interesting that the
ancient word for meditation

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:37.000
comes from the word which means
"to do something over and over until you get used to it."

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:51.680
And the idea, for example,
in the seven-part meditation preparation
which we did in the last segment--

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:08.280
if you appreciate and express your gratitude to your teacher over and over in the meditation,

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:14.760
then that will become a habit.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:22.880
And your mind will change, and you will
become a person who is more grateful to other people.

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:33.160
Okay, now the other factor that Vasabandhu mentions in the ancient Abhidharma teaching:

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:46.800
ngun che kang yin (SNGON BYAS GANG YIN). Also, a factor is: which seed did you plant before the other one?

00:20:51.800 --> 00:21:03.120
I spent years working through this explanation of three factors that cause the seed to open first,
I spent years working through this explanation of three factors that cause the seed to open first,

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:12.160
and four factors that cause the seed open first,
because we want to be sure to make a
good seed open first when we die.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:34.840
So, if you really studied these quotations, in my opinion,

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:40.360
you have to read it this way. Okay, here we go.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:49.040
Four factors which decide which
karma's going to open first when you die.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:58.040
Okay, then first rule, generally speaking,

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:04.040
generally speaking,

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:11.680
the seed that you planted first will open first.
First in/first out in accounting system.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:28.440
And that kind of makes sense.
So I always remember this big lie I did when I was a kid.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:37.640
Only once in my whole life I stole money--

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:45.680
from my mother. I stole five dollars when I was young.

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:51.360
And so, let's say later when I was in the
diamond business,

00:22:53.040 --> 00:23:07.000
suppose I wasn't honest on my taxes--although I was. So, let's say theoretically I cheated on tax.

00:23:10.640 --> 00:23:16.320
So, it makes sense, at the time of my death,

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:27.000
if those two seeds haven't opened yet,
which one will open first?

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:35.080
Yeah, the first one I did when I was a kid.
So, that makes sense.

00:23:36.120 --> 00:23:45.840
First in/first out.  Now, second factor.
And I'm interpreting these two quotations.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:54.040
Let's say in my diamond career for 19 years,

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:01.640
I cheated on my taxes every year,

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:12.640
19 times, and it kind of covered my whole 19-year career,
which it *did not* by the way.

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:22.680
So, you have one lie to my mom when I was a kid,

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:39.120
then you have a cheating on my taxes over and over, which takes about six months preparation, for 19 years.

00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:50.520
And if those seeds--karmas--didn't open yet,

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:57.560
when I die, which one will be triggered first?

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:04.640
Yeah, 19 years of cheating,

00:25:07.240 --> 00:25:12.480
even though it came after the lie when I was a kid.

00:25:18.120 --> 00:25:32.000
Now, third factor.
What if I'm in the hospital and I'm dying,

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:40.520
and don't forget in Buddhism, dying is not really an end.

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:56.040
My rough consciousness dies, and then I
go to a very very primordial ancient consciousness--subtle consciousness.

00:25:59.840 --> 00:26:10.200
So, in the moment of that transition of my mind--
from being aware of this world

00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:17.520
to the ancient, ancient stream of mind which
I have had for billions of years.

00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:28.840
So, in that delicate moment of the last ability of
my mind to have a normal thought,

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:49.280
what if in that moment my family is crying,
and they grab my arm, "Don't go, don't go!"

00:26:53.600 --> 00:26:59.880
Then my mind is almost dying to a subtle level.

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:13.040
I can't even recognize who's grabbing my arm.
Is it my kid or my wife,

00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:24.080
but I feel this grabbing of my arm and then suddenly I remember a fight I had when I was a teenager

00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:30.600
when someone grabbed my arm and I hit them.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:35.080
So, in that subtle minute--

00:27:37.080 --> 00:27:43.720
when my mind is going from this life mind
back to my subtle mind--

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:56.040
in that moment someone grabs my arm and I feel this hatred that I felt when I was a teenager.

00:28:01.120 --> 00:28:06.000
Then that one's [karmic seed]
going to cancel the two other ones.

00:28:08.160 --> 00:28:19.240
Forget the lie when you're a kid.
Forget the cheating on your tax,
even though it went on for 19 years.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:31.040
In that crucial moment, if you feel intense anger,

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:35.720
guess which seed will open?

00:28:36.800 --> 00:28:43.840
Yeah, the one where you hit the guy.
And we'll talk more about that.

00:28:44.440 --> 00:28:54.400
But obviously it's very important that people die
in a very conducive peaceful atmosphere.

00:29:01.120 --> 00:29:14.360
And if we are their relatives, we have to be careful ...
we have to make sure they die in a peaceful way.

00:29:18.280 --> 00:29:21.040
The room should be peaceful.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:29.600
The people standing around are sad,
but they are not making loud frightening noises.

00:29:34.800 --> 00:29:38.120
Okay now, the fourth one.

00:29:38.760 --> 00:29:46.000
So far we had some lie I did when I was a small kid,

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:55.160
and normally that one should open first;
at death, for example.

00:29:56.280 --> 00:30:05.000
But, if I did a similar lying but over and over for 19 years,

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:15.920
then that karma will come to the front
of the line ahead of the kid karma.

00:30:23.880 --> 00:30:32.600
And that will decide where I go in my next life.
But in the moment that was supposed to open

00:30:34.520 --> 00:30:41.320
someone grabbed my arm and I got a big anger,

00:30:41.320 --> 00:30:50.760
then now that super hot anger at the
last moment will take priority.

00:30:53.960 --> 00:31:00.680
Unless there was a very heavy karma in my mind.

00:31:01.160 --> 00:31:09.520
You know, like I went to a war and I was
struggling with another soldier

00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:16.840
and I consciously pointed the gun
at their head and I shot.

00:31:21.840 --> 00:31:30.760
That one is so much more serious than lying to my mother, than nineteen years of cheating on my taxes,

00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:35.040
than someone grabbing my arm at the last moment.

00:31:41.640 --> 00:31:48.040
Then that killing karma is obviously going to first ...
to the front of the line.

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:55.000
So, this is the one that makes sense to me--
how to read those verses.

00:32:00.640 --> 00:32:05.320
Let's review and we'll stop this segment.
Let's review and we'll stop this segment.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:16.080
And next segment we are going to practice dying ...
but not exactly okay?

00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:28.760
Generally speaking, if I did it earlier--
I lied to my mom when I was a kid--

00:32:29.200 --> 00:32:42.760
then generally,  that one should open first. Unless ...
later in my life I did some kind of lie for 19 years,

00:32:45.160 --> 00:32:53.920
now that one should open
at the moment of death and decide where I go.

00:32:55.200 --> 00:33:02.880
Unless, someone grabs my arm while I'm dying

00:33:03.320 --> 00:33:12.600
and suddenly I remember some violent day.
Then that one will move to the front of the line.

00:33:14.720 --> 00:33:25.640
Unless, in my whole life I did some very, very serious bad deed, like killing another human being.

00:33:28.040 --> 00:33:33.920
So, that's our review of
where we stopped in the last retreat,

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:42.920
and we're ready to move on to segment number four.

00:33:44.200 --> 00:33:48.720
Thank you, and thank you Stanley for translating.

